ue}{suffix}.\", \"reasoning\": \"The suffix slot's gate is number line, which this lc may use, so it prints on the number line. The family therefore asks for a placement on a number line.\"}, \"block_or_bar_models\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"Use base-10 blocks to show the number {total}.\", \"reasoning\": \"Base-10 blocks are the block model named by the clause. F17 asks the learner to show a number with them. No family prints a bar model, but the block model is covered.\"}, \"numerals\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F14\", \"template\": \"Move the dot to show {value}{suffix}.\", \"reasoning\": \"The value slot prints the generated number as digits, so the learner reads and works with numerals.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F04\", \"F06\", \"F07\", \"F08\", \"F09\", \"F10\", \"F11\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Add the parts together to get {number}.\", \"Add the value of every block together to get the total, {number}.\", \"Identify each word part and its {pv_label}.\", \"Multiply each block's own value by how many there are, then add all the totals together.\", \"{capitalize}: {expanded_form}.\", \"{chunk}-{v}\", \"{p0}\", \"{v} hundred\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F03, F04 and F07 are hints whose text names operations the vocabulary lists as NOT_YET_KNOWN: F03 and F04 use the word Add, and F07 uses Multiply and add. F04 and F07 are chosen by task_type, but F03 is always printed. F08 prints the plus sign between parts in its expanded_form domain (a repeats-a-generated-value slot with a printed list), which implies addition, a NOT_YET_KNOWN operation. F06 nests F02, whose only printed text is 'value of each part' (the place value gate is always closed for this lc), so F06 always prints the garbled hint Identify each word part and its value of each part. F09's chunk domain includes an empty member, so the template can print a bare dash or a tens word with no ones word. F10's p0 domain includes empty members, so an empty answer choice can print. F11's v domain includes an empty member, so a choice reading only the word hundred can print. These are misleading or unreadable learner text, and the lc's gates are breached in each case. F01, F02, F05, F12, F13, F14, F15, F16, F17 and F18 show no fault within the lc's vocabulary and range.\"}",
